---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DarkHeader from '../../components/DarkHeader.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="What a dollar buys in an EV right now | Cooper Minehart"
  description="171 electric vehicle configurations across nine markets plotted by usable kWh and driving range against retail MSRP, with toggles for region and cell chemistry."
>
  <DarkHeader>
    <div class="max-w-[864px] mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-10">
      <a href="/blog" class="text-sm text-forest-400 hover:text-forest-300 mb-6 inline-block">← Blog</a>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-3">What a dollar buys in an EV right now</h1>
      <p class="text-stone-300 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        EV kWh and range plotted against MSRP.
      </p>
    </div>
  </DarkHeader>

  <article class="max-w-[864px] mx-auto px-6 pt-10 pb-24 text-[#1E2A33]">
    <div class="space-y-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#1E2A33]">
      <p>
        I spend a lot of time thinking about how much it costs to buy a kWh of battery storage, and got curious what it looks like at the vehicle level.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="evp-fig" data-evp-fig="us-kwh">
      <div class="evp-chips"></div>
      <div class="evp-wrap">
        <svg role="img" aria-label="Usable battery kWh versus retail MSRP for US market electric vehicles"></svg>
        <div class="evp-tip" hidden></div>
      </div>
      <div class="evp-live" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#1E2A33]">
      <p>
        The returning 2027 Chevy Bolt LT is $27,600 for 65 kWh of usable LFP, or GM will also sell you a 212 kWh usable NCMA Hummer EV for $114,800.
      </p>
      <p>
        Kia's new EV3 Long Range gives you 78 kWh for $34,990, and five dollars further right the Chevy Equinox EV LT gives you 85 kWh for $34,995. Above $50,000, GM's Silverado EV Work Truck trims take three frontier steps in a row (119, 170, and 205 kWh usable), and the Hummer charges an extra $40,600 for the last 7 kWh. The VinFast VF 9 (123 kWh at $69,800) and Rivian R1T Dual Max (141.5 kWh at $83,900) are other massive-capacity-contenders.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you turn on the global markets, China takes every single Pareto step below $50k before handing the frontier straight back to good old full-size pickups. I really wanted the US to be cost-competitive, or for us to be competing for entirely different markets, but we're still a little behind on this metric (and we're subsidizing and they're subsidizing so who knows what actual cost to build is).
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="evp-fig" data-evp-fig="global-chem">
      <div class="evp-chips"></div>
      <div class="evp-wrap">
        <svg role="img" aria-label="Global usable battery kWh versus retail MSRP across regions and emerging battery chemistries"></svg>
        <div class="evp-tip" hidden></div>
      </div>
      <div class="evp-live" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#1E2A33]">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[#1E2A33] pt-4">
        equal-range basis
      </h2>
      <p>
        Changing the vertical axis from usable kWh to EPA combined miles knocks the Equinox EV, Mustang Mach-E, standard-pack Silverado, and Hummer off the curve. The Model 3 Long Range RWD ($42,490, 363 miles), the two-speed 800V Mercedes CLA 250+ ($47,950, 374 miles from 85 kWh), BMW's iX3 ($61,500, 399 miles), and the Lucid Air Grand Touring ($114,900, 512 miles from 112 kWh, beating the 212 kWh Hummer by 145 miles on roughly half the battery) take their spots.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="evp-fig" data-evp-fig="us-range">
      <div class="evp-chips"></div>
      <div class="evp-wrap">
        <svg role="img" aria-label="Driving range in miles versus retail MSRP across EPA and global test cycles"></svg>
        <div class="evp-tip" hidden></div>
      </div>
      <div class="evp-live" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#1E2A33]">
      <p>
        What I really want to know (and conveniently, what I get paid to do) is how much each of these cost to build, how much each part costs to build, and how much/where incentives are applied to each. Unfortunately this alone doesn't tell us.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-6 mb-8 evp-bleed">
      <div class="border-2 border-[#1E2A33] bg-white">
        <iframe
          src="/maps/ev-pareto/index.html?embed=1"
          title="EV battery kWh and range versus MSRP interactive explorer"
          class="w-full block"
          style="height: 1120px; border: 0;"
          id="evp-tool"
        />
      </div>
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#1E2A33]">
      <p>
        A few caveats on the numbers. I didn't want to dig too hard so MSRPs exclude destination fees, dealer markups, and purchase incentives, and non-USD prices convert at fixed November 2026 rates. Where an automaker only publishes gross pack kWh, usable capacity is estimated from teardown or EV Database discharge data. You can grab the raw audited dataset <a href="/maps/ev-pareto/vehicles.json" download class="text-[#2C4FA3] underline">here (JSON)</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-[#E3E8EA] text-sm text-[#56636D] leading-relaxed">
      <p>Coop</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <script is:inline src="/maps/ev-pareto/model.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="/maps/ev-pareto/data.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="/maps/ev-pareto/post-charts.js"></script>
  <script is:inline>
    window.addEventListener('message', function (ev) {
      if (ev.data && ev.data.type === 'ev-pareto-height' && typeof ev.data.height === 'number') {
        var frame = document.getElementById('evp-tool');
        if (frame) frame.style.height = Math.max(820, ev.data.height + 8) + 'px';
      }
    });
  </script>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Archivo';
    src: url('/fonts/Archivo-400.ttf') format('truetype');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Archivo';
    src: url('/fonts/Archivo-600.ttf') format('truetype');
    font-weight: 600;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Archivo';
    src: url('/fonts/Archivo-800.ttf') format('truetype');
    font-weight: 800;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  .evp-fig {
    margin: 24px 0 32px;
    font-family: 'Archivo', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .evp-bleed {
    width: min(1360px, calc(100vw - 32px));
    position: relative;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }
  .evp-chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .evp-chip {
    font-family: 'Archivo', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 5px 10px;
    border: 1px solid #1E2A33;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: #FFFFFF;
    color: #1E2A33;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .evp-chip:hover,
  .evp-chip[aria-pressed="true"] {
    background: #1E2A33;
    color: #FFFFFF;
  }
  .evp-legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px 14px;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border: 1px solid #E3E8EA;
    border-bottom: 0;
    background: #FFFFFF;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    line-height: 16px;
    color: #1E2A33;
  }
  .evp-leg-item {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
  }
  .evp-leg-line {
    width: 16px;
    height: 2.5px;
    background: #D6363F;
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .evp-wrap {
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid #E3E8EA;
    border-top: 2px solid #1E2A33;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: #FFFFFF;
    padding: 8px 4px 4px;
  }
  .evp-wrap svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .evp-ax {
    font-family: 'Archivo', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: #56636D;
  }
  .evp-axt {
    font-family: 'Archivo', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: #1E2A33;
  }
  .evp-lab {
    font-family: 'Archivo', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    fill: #56636D;
    paint-order: stroke;
    stroke: #FFFFFF;
    stroke-width: 3.5px;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .evp-on {
    fill: #1E2A33;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .evp-pt {
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .evp-pt:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
  }
  .evp-focus-ring {
    fill: none;
    stroke: transparent;
  }
  .evp-pt:focus-visible .evp-focus-ring {
    stroke: #2C4FA3;
    stroke-width: 2px;
  }
  .evp-tip {
    position: absolute;
    pointer-events: none;
    background: #1E2A33;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    border: 2px solid #1E2A33;
    border-radius: 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 16px;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    max-width: 256px;
    z-index: 5;
  }
  .evp-tip-f {
    display: inline-block;
    background: #D6363F;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .evp-tip-hint {
    display: block;
    color: #C7D0D6;
    font-size: 10.5px;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .evp-live {
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 18px;
    color: #56636D;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .evp-pin-box {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    border: 1px solid #1E2A33;
    border-left: 4px solid #1E2A33;
    background: #FFFFFF;
    color: #1E2A33;
  }
  .evp-pin-box.is-frontier {
    border-left-color: #D6363F;
  }
  .evp-pin-main strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1E2A33;
  }
  .evp-pin-clear {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-family: 'Archivo', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    line-height: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 3px 8px;
    border: 1px solid #1E2A33;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: #FFFFFF;
    color: #1E2A33;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .evp-pin-clear:hover {
    background: #1E2A33;
    color: #FFFFFF;
  }
</style>
